106        title 'Golden note_freqfmtoutraw';
107        /* NOTE-freqfmtoutraw (qa tick191 F2): OUT= stores the RAW class value with the
108           format ATTACHED — never the formatted label STRING (a descriptor must not
109           disagree with the value it describes; a proc must not retype a column just
110           because it carries a format). Pinned through three surfaces: PRINT still
111           renders the labels, CONTENTS shows Num + the attached format, and a DATA-step
112           read-back does ARITHMETIC on the class var — the surface that proves the
113           type. The collapsed bf. arm proves SAS stores the LOWEST internal value of a
114           format-combined group (Base SAS 9.4 Procedures Guide, PROC MEANS CLASS stmt
115           Tip, printed p.1496). Siblings sharing the groupFormats rewrite are pinned
116           too: SUMMARY (same builder), FREQ OUT= (own builder, same bug), UNIVARIATE
117           (raw cells already; the format now attaches). The $cf. char-class control
118           must not move: its raw value already is a string. */
119        proc format;
120          value gf 1='One' 2='Two';
NOTE: Format GF has been output.
121          value bf low-2='Low' 3-high='High';
NOTE: Format BF has been output.
122          value $cf 'a'='Alpha' 'b'='Beta';
